{% extends 'pages/communities/sagamok/members-first-plan-layout.html.twig' %}
{% set plan_key = 'scorecard' %}{% set plan_short = 'Member scorecard' %}{% set plan_eyebrow = 'Quarterly accountability' %}
{% set plan_title = 'The scorecard members should receive every quarter' %}
{% set plan_description = 'Track each commitment from promise to result using the same status, budget, evidence, member-benefit and correction fields.' %}
{% set plan_status = 'Reporting standard' %}
{% block plan_content %}
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">One reporting rule</p><h2>Every priority reports the same six things.</h2></header><div class="plan-grid plan-grid--3"><div class="plan-card"><h3>Commitment</h3><p>Outcome, accountable office and due date.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Status</h3><p>Not started, on track, at risk, delayed or complete.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Money</h3><p>Approved, funding source, spent and forecast.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Delivery</h3><p>Milestone due, reached and evidence link.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Member benefit</h3><p>Who benefited, how and how it was measured.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Correction</h3><p>What changes next, by whom and by what date.</p></div></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Whole-plan dashboard</p><h2>The minimum measures across all eight priorities.</h2></header><div class="plan-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Priority</th><th>Delivery measures</th><th>Member-benefit measures</th><th>Control measure</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Member government</td><td>Records, decisions, minutes and appeals completed on time</td><td>Members participating and questions resolved</td><td>Overdue disclosures and unexplained refusals</td></tr><tr><td>Community wealth</td><td>Trust, lending, debt and withdrawal reconciliation</td><td>Jobs, homes, services, repayments and distributions</td><td>Policy exceptions and risk-limit breaches</td></tr><tr><td>Enterprises</td><td>Company reports, repayments, dividends and targets</td><td>Member jobs, training, procurement and strategic benefit</td><td>Correction plans and unreported risks</td></tr><tr><td>Homes and infrastructure</td><td>Lots, starts, completions, repairs and water reliability</td><td>Wait-list movement and households served</td><td>Budget and schedule variance</td></tr><tr><td>Health, families and Elders</td><td>Access, referrals, follow-up and home supports</td><td>Needs met and avoidable gaps reduced</td><td>Cases outside service standard</td></tr><tr><td>Language, culture and learning</td><td>Teaching hours, learners, programs and progression</td><td>Everyday language use and family participation</td><td>Cancelled delivery and succession gaps</td></tr><tr><td>Lands, safety and rights</td><td>Reviews, conditions, monitoring and safety actions</td><td>Rights protected and agreed benefits received</td><td>Overdue conditions and threshold events</td></tr><tr><td>Public service</td><td>Vacancies, hiring, service standards and audit actions</td><td>Faster, clearer and more reliable services</td><td>Long acting roles and overdue controls</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Status rules</p><h2>Make red and yellow mean something.</h2></header><div class="plan-grid"><div class="plan-card"><h3>At risk</h3><p>A milestone, funding source, capacity assumption or external dependency may prevent delivery. The report names the risk and response.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Delayed</h3><p>The approved date has been missed. The report gives the cause, new date, accountable owner and corrective action.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Complete</h3><p>The promised output exists, the evidence is linked, actual cost is reported and member benefit is measured.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Stopped or changed</h3><p>The report states why, who decided, what money remains and what replaces the commitment.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="plan-decision"><h2>Members see the record, not a performance grade.</h2><p>The scorecard does not hide weak results inside a single percentage. It shows the commitment, evidence, money, variance and correction so members can judge the result themselves.</p></section>
